// EXPECT: [E012]
// EXPECT-TEXT: Error Ln 7, Col 12: `as|` says what happens at an integer type's ends, and 'f32' is a float: write `as`.
// I.161: `as|`, `as?` and `as%` name what happens at an integer type's ends, and a float has none:
// IEEE 754 defines every conversion to a float, an infinity past its range. They emitted the plain
// conversion and promised a clamp, a check or a wrap that never happened.
func f(n i64) f32 {
    return n as| f32
}

func main() i32 { return 0 }
